  "rationale": "Deploying mfa:admin alone is enough. Every exfiltration technique needs admin on db, fileserver or backup. Those need a foothold there, which requires stolen_dbadmin. The only sources of stolen_dbadmin are dump_dbadmin_dc and dump_dbadmin_adfs, which need admin_dc or admin_adfs. Those in turn need foothold_dc or foothold_adfs, obtainable only via auth_dc or auth_adfs, both of which require NOT mfa_admin. With mfa:admin deployed, that whole chain is cut. Zero controls fails because the attack succeeds undefended: phish, pivot, auth_appserver, kerberoast, auth_dc, escalate_dc, dump_dbadmin, auth_db, escalate_db, exfiltrate_db. So the minimum is 1."
